[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
casa-ui runs from %%RELEASE%% behind a reverse proxy, as the
www user by default. It needs the CouchDB from databases/couchdb3
running with an admin, and an operator key enrolled on the casa
cluster.

To set it up:

 1. Give it a config, a key and the control nodes' certificates, in one
    of two ways.

    To share the files casa-ui uses from a casa checkout, in your own
    ~/.config/casa/, run the daemon as yourself and point it there:

      sysrc casa_ui_user=you casa_ui_group=you
      sysrc casa_ui_config=/home/you/.config/casa/ui.ucl

    The daemon and mix phx.server then use the same key and CouchDB
    login, and listen on the same address, so run one at a time.
    Restart the daemon after mix casa.couchdb.reset, which writes a new
    password into ui.ucl.

    To keep it apart as the www user, make it a key and enrol it from a
    host that may run casa operator commands:

      casa key gen --operator ui
      casa operator add ui ~/.config/casa/operator.crt

    Put the key and certificate in %%ETCDIR%%/ui/ as ui.key and
    ui.crt, with each control node's certificate, owned by www and
    readable by www only. Then copy %%ETCDIR%%/ui.ucl.sample to
    %%ETCDIR%%/ui.ucl and set the CouchDB URL, the listen address
    and the control nodes in it.

 2. Set PHX_HOST, the host name the proxy serves, in casa_ui_env.
    The proxy must pass X-Forwarded-Proto.

      sysrc casa_ui_env="PHX_HOST=casa.example.org"

 3. Enable the services and start them:

      service couchdb3 enable
      service couchdb3 start
      service casa_ui enable
      service casa_ui start
EOM
}
]
